- Single-source-to-directory: destination resolved to `DIR/basename`
- No parent creation; missing parents reported as errors
- Per-source failure isolation: continue after errors, exit 1 if any failed
- Source symlinks followed to regular files; directory sources rejected
- Destination symlinks followed; dangling destination symlinks rejected
- Self-copy (including hard-link/inode aliasing) rejected before any write
- Existing destination overwritten with permissions retained
- New file created with `source_mode & ~umask` (via kernel umask on `.mode()`)
- Arbitrary non-NUL pathname bytes preserved via `OsString`/`Path`
- No panics on ordinary I/O errors; all errors propagated as `io::Result`
- `copy_path` is the semantic anchor, called directly from `main`

